# m95 persistent boot logger (R/vendor).
#
# WHY: no UART on this device, USB bulk is flaky, ram_console keeps only the
# kernel tail, and dropbox only records completed boots. A boot that hangs on
# the animation leaves ZERO framework logs behind. This service streams all
# logcat buffers to /cache (rotation 4x4MB, survives reboot, readable from
# TWRP) starting at post-fs-data — early enough to catch system_server,
# surfaceflinger and HAL crash loops, late enough that /cache is mounted
# (fstab.mt6797 mounts it with wait,check before post-fs-data completes).
# Runs under permissive bring-up; sepolicy narrowing comes with enforcing.
# Disable by removing from PRODUCT_PACKAGES (no code depends on it).

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /cache/m95-bootlog 0770 system log
    start m95_bootlog

service m95_bootlog /system/bin/logcat -b all -v threadtime -f /cache/m95-bootlog/boot.txt -r 4096 -n 4
    class late_start
    user logd
    group logd system
    disabled
